      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Quick Start Guide: NebulaFlow Deployment Tool**\n\n**Step 1: Login to NebulaFlow**\n\nTo begin, authenticate with NebulaFlow using your token:\n```bash\nnf auth login --token <TOKEN>\n```\nReplace `<TOKEN>` with your actual NebulaFlow token.\n\n**Step 2: Initialize a New Cluster**\n\nCreate a new cluster with the desired region and size:\n```bash\nnf cluster init --region us-east-1 --size small\n```\nThis command will create a new cluster in the specified region with a small instance size.\n\n**Step 3: Deploy Your Application**\n\nDeploy your application configuration to the cluster:\n```bash\nnf deploy --config ./production.yaml\n```\nReplace `./production.yaml` with the path to your actual application configuration file.\n\nThat's it! You should now have a running NebulaFlow cluster with your application deployed.",
